       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the maximum is 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCan you check what was intended? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release. 1700 mg may be a mix-up with 850 mg.\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **1700 mg total per day.** This would be split into doses such as 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Some other dose.** If you meant something different, or you have a reason for this dose, tell me.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
