     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Metformin 5,100 mg/day is twice the labeled maximum, and I don't know of a clinical scenario where that dose is appropriate. It could cause serious harm, including lactic acidosis, and a patient with normal kidney and liver function is still at risk.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n- 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- A lower starting dose, such as 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, then titrate\n\nIf you think this dose is needed, please talk to the attending or clinical pharmacy first. If you tell me they approved it, or give me the documented rationale, I can add that to the order note. Even then, I'd want the order to go through the hospital's normal override and verification process, not be entered by me as a routine order."
      }
